{"name":"Shin Godzilla","hex":"#9a373f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The front part of the leg below the knee; the front edge of the shin bone:  Shinbone on  Wikipedia.Wikipedia","A fishplate for a railway"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To climb up or lower oneself down a mast, tree, rope, or the like, by embracing it alternately with the arms and legs, without help of steps, spurs, or the like.","To strike with the shin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shin Godzilla","blocks":[{"text":"Shin Godzilla  is a 2016 Japanese kaiju film directed by Hideaki Anno and Shinji Higuchi, with a screenplay by Anno and visual effects by Higuchi. Produced by Toho Pictures and Cine Bazar and distributed by Toho Co., Ltd., it is the 31st film in the Godzilla franchise, the 29th film produced by Toho, Toho's third reboot of the franchise, and the first film in the franchise's Reiwa era. It is the first reboot of a tokusatsu series to be adapted by Anno and Higuchi, followed by Shin Ultraman (2022) and Shin Kamen Rider (2023). The film stars Hiroki Hasegawa, Yutaka Takenouchi, and Satomi Ishihara. In the film, politicians struggle with bureaucratic red tape in order to deal with the sudden appearance of an ever-evolving monster named Godzilla."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/02/Shin_Godzilla.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shin_Godzilla"},{"title":"Shin Godzilla (character)","blocks":[{"text":"Shin Godzilla is a giant monster, or kaiju, in Toho Co., Ltd.'s Godzilla media franchise. An iteration of Godzilla, it first appeared in the 2016 reboot film of the same name, released by Toho and co-directed by Hideaki Anno and Shinji Higuchi."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/57/Shin_Godzilla_-_Godzilla%27s_4th_Form.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shin_Godzilla_(character)"},{"title":"Godzilla","blocks":[{"text":"Godzilla is a fictional giant monster, or daikaijū, that first appeared in the 1954 film of the same name, directed by Ishirō Honda. The character has since become an international pop culture icon, appearing in various media: 33 Japanese films by Toho, five American films, and numerous video games, novels, comic books, and television shows. Godzilla has been dubbed the King of the Monsters, an epithet first used in Godzilla, King of the Monsters! (1956), the American localization of the 1954 film."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Godzilla_%281954%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Godzilla_%281954%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Godzilla"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Godzilla_Resurgence_World_Premiere_Red_Carpet-_Hasegawa_Hiroki.jpg/500px-Godzilla_Resurgence_World_Premiere_Red_Carpet-_Hasegawa_Hiroki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Godzilla_Resurgence_World_Premiere_Red_Carpet-_Hasegawa_Hiroki.jpg/1280px-Godzilla_Resurgence_World_Premiere_Red_Carpet-_Hasegawa_Hiroki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Godzilla_Resurgence_World_Premiere_Red_Carpet-_Hasegawa_Hiroki.jpg/500px-Godzilla_Resurgence_World_Premiere_Red_Carpet-_Hasegawa_Hiroki.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGodzilla_Resurgence_World_Premiere_Red_Carpet-_Hasegawa_Hiroki.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Godzilla_Resurgence_World_Prem